ame from the people went  through some of the same things that  they're going through and it's like a  dialogue that you have with the author I  think you have a much more human  relationship to a printed book than you  do to one that's on a screen people want  the experience of holding it of turning  the page of marking their progress in a  story and then you have of all things  the smell of a book fresh ink on paper  or the aging paper smell you don't  really get that from anything else the  book itself you know can't be turned off  with a switch it's a story that you can  hold in your hand and carry around with  you and that's part of what makes them  so valuable and I think will make them  valuable for for the duration a shelf of  books frankly is made to outlast you no  matter who you are  [Music]
 

